{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WrdJfFgLmoTAydrG6JjX2D","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd002-sys\n2\ttitle: \"pkg/sys: Syscall Abstractions\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Four utilities (ls, du, find, xargs) need OS-level capabilities that Go's standard\n6\t  library does not expose in a portable, stable form: terminal-width queries, extended\n7\t  file metadata (hard-link count, device and inode numbers, physical block counts),\n8\t  and signal handling for SIGPIPE and SIGWINCH. On Darwin and Linux these syscalls\n9\t  diverge in struct layout (st_mtimespec vs st_mtim, st_blocks interpretation) and\n10\t  available interfaces (TIOCGWINSZ ioctl). Without pkg/sys each cmd/ package would\n11\t  import syscall or golang.org/x/sys directly, duplicating the Darwin/Linux divergence\n12\t  handling and making it harder to test or audit the syscall surface.\n13\t\n14\t  pkg/sys provides a stable, tested interface for these three capability areas. Each\n15\t  capability is driven by at least one concrete utility requirement derived from C source\n16\t  analysis (see dependency-map.yaml).\n17\t\n18\tgoals:\n19\t  - G1: Provide a portable terminal-width query and SIGPIPE handler that work on Darwin and Linux without cgo.\n20\t  - G2: Expose extended file metadata (st_nlink, st_uid, st_gid, st_rdev, st_blocks, st_ino, st_dev) not available from os.FileInfo.\n21\t  - G3: Provide a SIGWINCH handler that calls a user-supplied callback when the terminal is resized.\n22\t\n23\trequirements:\n24\t  R1:\n25\t    title: Terminal width and TTY detection\n26\t    items:\n27\t      - R1.1:\n28\t          text: Must provide func TerminalWidth() (int, error) that returns the current terminal column count by calling ioctl(TIOCGWINSZ) on stdout. Returns an error (not panic) when stdout is not a terminal or when ioctl fails.\n29\t      - R1.2:\n30\t          text: Must use golang.org/x/sys/unix (the project's only external dependency) to perform the TIOCGWINSZ ioctl; must not shell out to tput or stty and must not import golang.org/x/term.\n31\t      - R1.3:\n32\t          text: |\n33\t            Must provide func IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool that returns true when the file\n34\t            descriptor refers to a terminal, and false otherwise. Implementation: call\n35\t            golang.org/x/sys/unix.IoctlGetWinsize(int(fd), unix.TIOCGWINSZ) and return\n36\t            err == nil. Returns false for pipes, regular files, and non-terminal descriptors.\n37\t            The caller (pkg/format ColorEnabled) is responsible for extracting the fd from an\n38\t            io.Writer via type assertion to *os.File. Required by pkg/format to suppress color\n39\t            output when stdout is redirected.\n40\t      - R1.4:\n41\t          text: 'Utility context — ls (ls.c:2281): ls uses struct winsize to determine column count for its default multi-column layout and for the -w/--width flag default.'\n42\t      - R1.5:\n43\t          text: |\n44\t            Must provide func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() that installs a SIGPIPE handler causing the\n45\t            process to exit 0 when stdout or stderr is closed by a downstream consumer.\n46\t            Implementation: use signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE) with a buffered channel of\n47\t            size 1; in a dedicated goroutine call os.Exit(0) when the channel receives. Must not\n48\t            use signal.Ignore so that deferred cleanup functions do not run on SIGPIPE (matching\n49\t            GNU behavior where SIGPIPE terminates silently).\n50\t      - R1.6:\n51\t          text: InstallSIGPIPEHandler must be safe to call multiple times; only one goroutine per invocation is started.\n52\t      - R1.7:\n53\t          text: 'Utility context — ls (ls.c:1600-1620): ls installs a SIGPIPE handler via sigaction so that piping ls output to head does not produce a broken-pipe error message. du, find, and xargs have the same requirement.'\n54\t\n55\t  R2:\n56\t    title: Extended file metadata\n57\t    items:\n58\t      - R2.1:\n59\t          text: Must provide func Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error) and func Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error). Stat follows symbolic links (equivalent to os.Stat); Lstat does not follow symbolic links (equivalent to os.Lstat). Both return a *FileInfo populated from syscall.Stat_t.\n60\t      - R2.2:\n61\t          text: |\n62\t            FileInfo must be defined as the following named struct in package sys:\n63\t\n64\t              type FileInfo struct {\n65\t                  Mode    os.FileMode // file mode and type bits (from syscall.Stat_t.Mode)\n66\t                  Size    int64       // apparent file size in bytes (st_size)\n67\t                  Nlink   uint64      // hard-link count (st_nlink)\n68\t                  Uid     uint32      // owner user ID (st_uid)\n69\t                  Gid     uint32      // owner group ID (st_gid)\n70\t                  Rdev    uint64      // device ID for special files (st_rdev)\n71\t                  Dev     uint64      // device ID of the containing filesystem (st_dev)\n72\t                  Ino     uint64      // inode number (st_ino)\n73\t                  Blocks  int64       // number of 512-byte blocks allocated (st_blocks)\n74\t                  Blksize int64       // preferred I/O block size (st_blksize)\n75\t                  ModTime time.Time   // modification time (st_mtime / st_mtimespec)\n76\t                  Info    os.FileInfo // underlying os.FileInfo for os package compatibility\n77\t              }\n78\t      - R2.3:\n79\t          text: Must abstract the Darwin/Linux divergence in struct field names (st_mtimespec on Darwin vs st_mtim on Linux; st_blocks interpretation) so callers use a single API regardless of target platform.\n80\t      - R2.4:\n81\t          text: 'Utility context — ls (ls.c:213, 371): ls needs Nlink, Uid, Gid, Rdev, Mode for -l format; Blocks for -s; Ino for -i.'\n82\t      - R2.5:\n83\t          text: 'Utility context — du (du.c:554): du needs Dev and Ino for hard-link deduplication, and Blocks for physical block-count accumulation.'\n84\t      - R2.6:\n85\t          text: 'Utility context — find (find/ftsfind.c:172): find predicates (-type, -size, -newer, -perm, -uid, -gid) require Mode, Size, ModTime, Uid, Gid, Nlink from the stat struct.'\n86\t\n87\t  R3:\n88\t    title: SIGWINCH handling\n89\t    items:\n90\t      - R3.1:\n91\t          text: |\n92\t            Must provide func OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int)) that registers a SIGWINCH handler. When the terminal is resized, the handler calls TerminalWidth() and invokes the callback with the new width. If TerminalWidth() returns an error the callback is not invoked.\n93\t      - R3.2:\n94\t          text: Must support multiple calls to OnTerminalResize; each registered callback must be called on resize. Callbacks are called in registration order.\n95\t      - R3.3:\n96\t          text: 'Utility context — ls (ls.c:2281, SIGWINCH registration): ls re-queries terminal width on SIGWINCH to re-format output when the terminal window is resized during a long listing.'\n97\t\n98\tnon_goals:\n99\t  - pkg/sys does not wrap all of syscall or golang.org/x/sys; it exposes only the surfaces required by the current utility batch.\n100\t  - pkg/sys does not provide file-watching or inotify/kqueue interfaces.\n101\t  - pkg/sys does not handle SIGUSR1/SIGUSR2 (find's debug output); those are deferred to the find SRD.\n102\t  - pkg/sys does not provide process-group or terminal control (TIOCGPGRP, tcsetpgrp); those are deferred to the xargs SRD.\n103\t\n104\tpackage_contract:\n105\t  exports:\n106\t    - name: FileInfo\n107\t      signature: \"type FileInfo struct { Mode os.FileMode; Size int64; Nlink uint64; Uid uint32; Gid uint32; Rdev uint64; Dev uint64; Ino uint64; Blocks int64; Blksize int64; ModTime time.Time; AccessTime time.Time; ChangeTime time.Time; Info os.FileInfo }\"\n108\t    - name: Stat\n109\t      signature: \"func Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)\"\n110\t    - name: Lstat\n111\t      signature: \"func Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)\"\n112\t    - name: TerminalWidth\n113\t      signature: \"func TerminalWidth() (int, error)\"\n114\t    - name: IsTerminal\n115\t      signature: \"func IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool\"\n116\t    - name: InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n117\t      signature: \"func InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\"\n118\t    - name: OnTerminalResize\n119\t      signature: \"func OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))\"\n120\t  imports:\n121\t    - os\n122\t    - os/signal\n123\t    - syscall\n124\t    - time\n125\t    - golang.org/x/sys/unix\n126\t  import_constraints:\n127\t    - \"Must not import any cmd/ package.\"\n128\t    - \"Must not import any other pkg/ package.\"\n129\t\n130\tacceptance_criteria:\n131\t  - id: AC1\n132\t    criterion: \"TerminalWidth() returns a positive integer when called in a test with a pseudo-terminal (golang.org/x/term's test helpers or os.Pipe() as a TTY substitute is acceptable).\"\n133\t    traces:\n134\t      - R1.1\n135\t      - R1.2\n136\t      - R1.3\n137\t      - R1.4\n138\t      - R1.5\n139\t      - R1.6\n140\t      - R1.7\n141\t  - id: AC2\n142\t    criterion: \"Stat() and Lstat() on a known file return FileInfo with correct Nlink, Uid, Gid, Dev, Ino, and Blocks values as confirmed by running stat(1) on the same file.\"\n143\t    traces:\n144\t      - R1.1\n145\t      - R1.2\n146\t      - R1.3\n147\t      - R1.4\n148\t      - R1.5\n149\t      - R1.6\n150\t      - R1.7\n151\t  - id: AC3\n152\t    criterion: \"Lstat() on a symlink returns the symlink's own st_mode (type bits show symlink), not the target's mode.\"\n153\t    traces:\n154\t      - R1.1\n155\t      - R1.2\n156\t      - R1.3\n157\t      - R1.4\n158\t      - R1.5\n159\t      - R1.6\n160\t      - R1.7\n161\t  - id: AC4\n162\t    criterion: \"InstallSIGPIPEHandler() causes a process writing to a broken pipe to exit 0 rather than printing a write error.\"\n163\t    traces:\n164\t      - R1.1\n165\t      - R1.5\n166\t      - R1.7\n167\t      - R2.1\n168\t      - R3.1\n169\t  - id: AC5\n170\t    criterion: \"All pkg/sys code compiles on both darwin/arm64 and linux/amd64 with no build errors and no cgo.\"\n171\t    traces:\n172\t      - R1.1\n173\t      - R1.5\n174\t      - R1.7\n175\t      - R2.1\n176\t      - R3.1\n177\t  - id: AC6\n178\t    criterion: \"All pkg/sys code compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n179\t    traces:\n180\t      - R1.1\n181\t      - R1.2\n182\t      - R1.3\n183\t      - R1.4\n184\t      - R1.5\n185\t      - R1.6\n186\t      - R1.7\n187\t      - R2.1\n188\t      - R2.2\n189\t      - R2.3\n190\t      - R2.4\n191\t      - R2.5\n192\t      - R2.6\n193\t      - R3.1\n194\t      - R3.2\n195\t      - R3.3\n196\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41c6567c-b00b-415a-bb35-66914a4110ae","uuid":"9b1db7fb-cb5b-4b8f-aa78-fc31d219b345","timestamp":"2026-05-13T22:04:53.558Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5071/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd002-sys.yaml","content":"id: srd002-sys\ntitle: \"pkg/sys: Syscall Abstractions\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Four utilities (ls, du, find, xargs) need OS-level capabilities that Go's standard\n  library does not expose in a portable, stable form: terminal-width queries, extended\n  file metadata (hard-link count, device and inode numbers, physical block counts),\n  and signal handling for SIGPIPE and SIGWINCH. On Darwin and Linux these syscalls\n  diverge in struct layout (st_mtimespec vs st_mtim, st_blocks interpretation) and\n  available interfaces (TIOCGWINSZ ioctl). Without pkg/sys each cmd/ package would\n  import syscall or golang.org/x/sys directly, duplicating the Darwin/Linux divergence\n  handling and making it harder to test or audit the syscall surface.\n\n  pkg/sys provides a stable, tested interface for these three capability areas. Each\n  capability is driven by at least one concrete utility requirement derived from C source\n  analysis (see dependency-map.yaml).\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Provide a portable terminal-width query and SIGPIPE handler that work on Darwin and Linux without cgo.\n  - G2: Expose extended file metadata (st_nlink, st_uid, st_gid, st_rdev, st_blocks, st_ino, st_dev) not available from os.FileInfo.\n  - G3: Provide a SIGWINCH handler that calls a user-supplied callback when the terminal is resized.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Terminal width and TTY detection\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: Must provide func TerminalWidth() (int, error) that returns the current terminal column count by calling ioctl(TIOCGWINSZ) on stdout. Returns an error (not panic) when stdout is not a terminal or when ioctl fails.\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Must use golang.org/x/sys/unix (the project's only external dependency) to perform the TIOCGWINSZ ioctl; must not shell out to tput or stty and must not import golang.org/x/term.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: |\n            Must provide func IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool that returns true when the file\n            descriptor refers to a terminal, and false otherwise. Implementation: call\n            golang.org/x/sys/unix.IoctlGetWinsize(int(fd), unix.TIOCGWINSZ) and return\n            err == nil. Returns false for pipes, regular files, and non-terminal descriptors.\n            The caller (pkg/format ColorEnabled) is responsible for extracting the fd from an\n            io.Writer via type assertion to *os.File. Required by pkg/format to suppress color\n            output when stdout is redirected.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: 'Utility context — ls (ls.c:2281): ls uses struct winsize to determine column count for its default multi-column layout and for the -w/--width flag default.'\n      - R1.5:\n          text: |\n            Must provide func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() that installs a SIGPIPE handler causing the\n            process to exit 0 when stdout or stderr is closed by a downstream consumer.\n            Implementation: use signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE) with a buffered channel of\n            size 1; in a dedicated goroutine call os.Exit(0) when the channel receives. Must not\n            use signal.Ignore so that deferred cleanup functions do not run on SIGPIPE (matching\n            GNU behavior where SIGPIPE terminates silently).\n      - R1.6:\n          text: InstallSIGPIPEHandler must be safe to call multiple times; only one goroutine per invocation is started.\n      - R1.7:\n          text: 'Utility context — ls (ls.c:1600-1620): ls installs a SIGPIPE handler via sigaction so that piping ls output to head does not produce a broken-pipe error message. du, find, and xargs have the same requirement.'\n\n  R2:\n    title: Extended file metadata\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: Must provide func Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error) and func Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error). Stat follows symbolic links (equivalent to os.Stat); Lstat does not follow symbolic links (equivalent to os.Lstat). Both return a *FileInfo populated from syscall.Stat_t.\n      - R2.2:\n          text: |\n            FileInfo must be defined as the following named struct in package sys:\n\n              type FileInfo struct {\n                  Mode    os.FileMode // file mode and type bits (from syscall.Stat_t.Mode)\n                  Size    int64       // apparent file size in bytes (st_size)\n                  Nlink   uint64      // hard-link count (st_nlink)\n                  Uid     uint32      // owner user ID (st_uid)\n                  Gid     uint32      // owner group ID (st_gid)\n                  Rdev    uint64      // device ID for special files (st_rdev)\n                  Dev     uint64      // device ID of the containing filesystem (st_dev)\n                  Ino     uint64      // inode number (st_ino)\n                  Blocks  int64       // number of 512-byte blocks allocated (st_blocks)\n                  Blksize int64       // preferred I/O block size (st_blksize)\n                  ModTime time.Time   // modification time (st_mtime / st_mtimespec)\n                  Info    os.FileInfo // underlying os.FileInfo for os package compatibility\n              }\n      - R2.3:\n          text: Must abstract the Darwin/Linux divergence in struct field names (st_mtimespec on Darwin vs st_mtim on Linux; st_blocks interpretation) so callers use a single API regardless of target platform.\n      - R2.4:\n          text: 'Utility context — ls (ls.c:213, 371): ls needs Nlink, Uid, Gid, Rdev, Mode for -l format; Blocks for -s; Ino for -i.'\n      - R2.5:\n          text: 'Utility context — du (du.c:554): du needs Dev and Ino for hard-link deduplication, and Blocks for physical block-count accumulation.'\n      - R2.6:\n          text: 'Utility context — find (find/ftsfind.c:172): find predicates (-type, -size, -newer, -perm, -uid, -gid) require Mode, Size, ModTime, Uid, Gid, Nlink from the stat struct.'\n\n  R3:\n    title: SIGWINCH handling\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: |\n            Must provide func OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int)) that registers a SIGWINCH handler. When the terminal is resized, the handler calls TerminalWidth() and invokes the callback with the new width. If TerminalWidth() returns an error the callback is not invoked.\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must support multiple calls to OnTerminalResize; each registered callback must be called on resize. Callbacks are called in registration order.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: 'Utility context — ls (ls.c:2281, SIGWINCH registration): ls re-queries terminal width on SIGWINCH to re-format output when the terminal window is resized during a long listing.'\n\nnon_goals:\n  - pkg/sys does not wrap all of syscall or golang.org/x/sys; it exposes only the surfaces required by the current utility batch.\n  - pkg/sys does not provide file-watching or inotify/kqueue interfaces.\n  - pkg/sys does not handle SIGUSR1/SIGUSR2 (find's debug output); those are deferred to the find SRD.\n  - pkg/sys does not provide process-group or terminal control (TIOCGPGRP, tcsetpgrp); those are deferred to the xargs SRD.\n\npackage_contract:\n  exports:\n    - name: FileInfo\n      signature: \"type FileInfo struct { Mode os.FileMode; Size int64; Nlink uint64; Uid uint32; Gid uint32; Rdev uint64; Dev uint64; Ino uint64; Blocks int64; Blksize int64; ModTime time.Time; AccessTime time.Time; ChangeTime time.Time; Info os.FileInfo }\"\n    - name: Stat\n      signature: \"func Stat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)\"\n    - name: Lstat\n      signature: \"func Lstat(path string) (*FileInfo, error)\"\n    - name: TerminalWidth\n      signature: \"func TerminalWidth() (int, error)\"\n    - name: IsTerminal\n      signature: \"func IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool\"\n    - name: InstallSIGPIPEHandler\n      signature: \"func InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\"\n    - name: OnTerminalResize\n      signature: \"func OnTerminalResize(callback func(width int))\"\n  imports:\n    - os\n    - os/signal\n    - syscall\n    - time\n    - golang.org/x/sys/unix\n  import_constraints:\n    - \"Must not import any cmd/ package.\"\n    - \"Must not import any other pkg/ package.\"\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"TerminalWidth() returns a positive integer when called in a test with a pseudo-terminal (golang.org/x/term's test helpers or os.Pipe() as a TTY substitute is acceptable).\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n      - R1.6\n      - R1.7\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"Stat() and Lstat() on a known file return FileInfo with correct Nlink, Uid, Gid, Dev, Ino, and Blocks values as confirmed by running stat(1) on the same file.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n      - R1.6\n      - R1.7\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"Lstat() on a symlink returns the symlink's own st_mode (type bits show symlink), not the target's mode.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n      - R1.6\n      - R1.7\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"InstallSIGPIPEHandler() causes a process writing to a broken pipe to exit 0 rather than printing a write error.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.5\n      - R1.7\n      - R2.1\n      - R3.1\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"All pkg/sys code compiles on both darwin/arm64 and linux/amd64 with no build errors and no cgo.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.5\n      - R1.7\n      - R2.1\n      - R3.1\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"All pkg/sys code compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n      - R1.6\n      - R1.7\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R2.5\n      - R2.6\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n","numLines":196,"startLine":1,"totalLines":196}}}
